{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"hexametral-peppery-wasp","creation_channel":"cli","description":"Two cheap, decoupled wins split out of the `doctor`/`fsck`/`validate` consolidation. The\nconsolidation itself is already tracked on epic `dabb-7d4b-f5bc-40e6` and is NOT duplicated here.\n\n**1. `validate --fix` is advertised in three places and does nothing.** `validate.py:361-362` is\nliterally `elif arg == \"--fix\": pass  # accepted, no-op (the bash --fix path is unimplemented)`.\nIt is documented in `--help` (`validate.py:342`), in `docs/cli-reference.md:458`, AND printed at\nruntime as the suggested remedy (`validate.py:309`, `:322`: \"Run with `--fix` to attempt automatic\nrepairs (interactive)\"). A user following the tool's own advice gets nothing, silently.\n\nMaintainer decision: remove it. `doctor` is the path for fixing.\n\n**2. `docs/chatgpt-agent-guide.md:91` sends agents to the wrong command.** It says to run\n\"`rebar validate` (or `rebar fsck`) against the tracker to confirm store integrity\" — but store\nintegrity is `fsck`'s job and is not something `validate` checks at all. `fsck` reads bytes and git\nrefs; `validate` reads reduced ticket semantics. They are cleanly disjoint.\n\nInvestigation confirmed the ambiguity has already cost real work: two epics (`dabb` and\n`18ae-4f54-a85b-4ddb`) were independently filed scoping the same `doctor` command, and `18ae` was\nclosed as a duplicate.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `--fix` is removed from `validate`'s parser, `--help`, `docs/cli-reference.md`, and both runtime hints\n- [ ] `docs/chatgpt-agent-guide.md:91` names the correct command for store integrity\n- [ ] Epic `dabb-7d4b-f5bc-40e6` is updated with this audit's findings (capability matrix, the no-op, the usage evidence that `doctor` is invoked by nothing)","id":"7be3-69af-6e84-4235","parent_id":"b5bc-f4f7-3433-4181","priority":3,"tags":["janitor"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Remove the no-op validate --fix and fix the wrong-command doc"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786047191150807001,"uuid":"a22d9b9c-e03b-41c7-bf95-de307b53f590"}